────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
1. YOUR 703 IS RIGHT
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The raw Flatiron tables give 1,700 and the RWDAP gives 703, and that gap is
fully explained — it isn't a discrepancy:

  1,700   2L docetaxel-only segment, raw FHRD
  1,632   of those, holding a row in t_enh_advancednsclc
    703   of those, advanced diagnosis on or after 2017-01-01   ← the whole gap

2017 is the RWDAP's own cohort-entry floor (protocol §3.2.1), which the raw
tables don't apply. Nothing else contributes: cohortn removes nobody, and the
regimen-string difference contributes zero.

Two honest caveats:
  • This reconciles COUNTS, not patient identity. The check that would show
    they're the same 703 people is written and hasn't run.
  • "1,700 2L docetaxel monotherapy" is loose — Flatiron admits a patient if
    ANY line-2 segment is exactly Docetaxel, which isn't the same as an
    exclusively-docetaxel second line.

Your censor filter reproduces the protocol's outcome gate exactly:
n = 703, of whom 691 have ≥3 months' follow-up and 12 have no OS.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
2. THE 18 COVARIATES — SOUND, THREE CHANGES
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Eight carry real evidence, counting publications where the factor was
prognostic AND multivariable-significant for OS AND in an advanced cohort:

  Sex (6) · ECOG (5) · Histology (4) · Age (3) · Albumin (3)
  Overall stage (2) · Race (2) · ALP (2)

The other ten sit at ≤1. Keep them, but as prediction inputs rather than
evidence-tier prognostic factors — the slide currently reads as evidence-ranked
and shouldn't.

ADD TWO:
  • Number of metastatic sites — evidence equal to stage and race, and NOT
    captured by initial overall stage. It's in REVEL's own baseline table.
  • Neutrophil count — stronger evidence than NLR, which currently absorbs it.
    The ratio hides the better signal.

EVALUATE, DON'T ADOPT YET:
  • Time since prior line (<9 vs ≥9 mo). A REVEL baseline field, but already
    substantially represented by time_1l_to_index, and both its anchor (start
    vs end of prior line) and the 9-month cut are unspecified. Adding it as
    written risks entering the same information twice at a different cut.

RECLASSIFY ONE, AND PLEASE DON'T DROP IT:
  • Smoking status — 24 publications, every advanced-setting multivariable
    estimate null. That's weak evidence for a prognostic claim, but it is not
    grounds to remove it. Prespecified adjustment covariates should be chosen
    from anticipated relevance and design considerations, not by counting
    significant results — selecting on observed significance is what the
    covariate-adjustment guidance warns against. The evidence tier is a label
    on the slide, not a decision rule.

FOUR PARAMETERISATIONS TO FIX:
  • Stage means the wrong thing. Flatiron holds stage at INITIAL diagnosis, not
    restaged at the 2L index, so it reads as de-novo vs recurrent. A coefficient
    fitted on that won't transfer to a trial's entry stage. Label it or drop it.
  • ECOG — don't collapse 2/3/4, and keep Unknown separate from Missing until
    we've seen the distribution. The numeric codebook is asserted from a spec we
    don't hold; a one-position offset would silently reclassify every ECOG 1.
  • Race — both supporting results are the Asian/Other-vs-White contrast, not
    White-vs-rest.
  • PD-L1 — currently blends two time-attribution methods, which makes the
    variable patient-dependent. Pick one as primary.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
3. OPTUM — NOT ANSWERABLE YET
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
I don't have an Optum sample size or covariate fill rates for you, and I'd
rather say that than give you a number I can't stand behind.

What HAS run against Optum is a deployment profile — corpus size, site
vocabulary, notes gate. What has NOT run is a 2L docetaxel cohort, so there is
no attrition funnel, no N, and no per-covariate completeness on that source.

The cohort builder is written and tested, but only against synthetic fixtures.
It has never been given a database connection. Two things gate it:

  • Optum's native line-of-therapy table can't be used. It's built from IV and
    procedure-coded records only, so a patient whose 1L was an oral (osimertinib,
    alectinib, lorlatinib) reads as 1L docetaxel instead of 2L. That's exactly
    the EGFR/ALK-positive group, whose prognosis differs — misassignment
    correlated with the outcome, inside a prognostic score. So we re-implement
    Flatiron's line rules on Optum source data instead.
  • That re-implementation is a rules-inspired reconstruction with documented
    substitutions, not a faithful reproduction. It hasn't been validated against
    Flatiron's own answer key yet. Until it has, I can't tell you an Optum N
    means the same thing as your Flatiron 703.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
4. TWO THINGS I NEED
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  • A terminology check, because it changes what we're building. "PS" is used
    for both prognostic score and propensity score in the source material.
    Protocol 308769 asks for a prognostic score — a regression on each patient's
    contribution to the covariate-adjusted log-rank statistic — which is a
    different object from a propensity score and isn't evaluated by a C-index.
    Worth confirming we mean the same thing before we freeze the covariate set.

  • SME sign-off. Everything above is analyst-level. The clinical adjudication
    column is empty on all 154 inventory rows, so none of these recommendations
    is clinically signed off yet.

One thing worth flagging for the analysis plan: eight of the ten strongest
covariates are collected in REVEL- and LUME-style trials under eligibility
restrictions that truncate their range. LUME-Lung 1 enrolled one PS-2 patient
of 1,314, so in-trial ECOG is effectively binary; stage is 100% IV in REVEL;
the organ-function labs are range-truncated by screening. How much prognostic
signal survives that is an empirical question — the direction isn't knowable in
advance and should be estimated, not assumed.

Happy to walk through any of this.
